This project is a fork of ubuntu-rockchip, originally created and maintained
by Joshua Riek (https://github.com/Joshua-Riek/ubuntu-rockchip).

The original project was archived by its maintainer. This fork continues
applying security updates and is maintained on a best-effort basis for
Orange Pi 5B hardware.

All upstream contributors retain copyright on their respective contributions.
The kernel, u-boot, and other components included in builds carry their own
licenses as documented in their respective source trees.

The desktop flavor builds and bundles WiiM Play
(https://github.com/shumatech/wiimplay) by ShumaTech, a UPnP control point for
WiiM music streamers, licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
It is compiled from source (pinned to v0.2) at image build time; ShumaTech and
its contributors retain copyright on that work.

The Bluetooth firmware loader brcm_patchram_plus shipped in /usr/bin/ is an
inherited binary (originally a Broadcom utility, distributed via Orange Pi's
orangepi-build), licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Broadcom, Orange Pi, and
its contributors retain copyright on that work. A rebuild from the current
published source is on the roadmap but is not yet viable (see
packages/brcm-patchram-plus/VALIDATION-FAILED.md).

